    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup is anchored today by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who provides our strongest projected efficiency with a score of 73.66. His matchup against G. Holmes is highly favorable, bolstered by a 17% boost for the pitcher's projected skill set and a 14% platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for counting stats. **Kyle Tucker** (61.68) also remains a core start; despite a tough matchup against Woo, the wind blowing out at the park provides a critical 5% tailwind to his output. While **Nasim Nunez** (56.96) and **Heliot Ramos** (58.59) are not the highest-scoring players, they remain essential, as our strategy prioritizes their elite sprint speed and base-stealing potential to attack the scarce stolen base category.\n\nRegarding bench decisions, **Luis Robert Jr.** (48.05) is the most notable \"marginal\" start, narrowly avoiding the bench. His raw talent was suppressed by a poor platoon dynamic against Perez (-15%), but his +4% efficiency boost gained from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery keeps him in the mix for a potential steal. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** (43.30) and **Jorge Polanco** (44.17) are skating on thin ice today, sitting near the lower limit of our start threshold. Both are plagued by a 32% rain risk in their respective games, and **Polanco** faces a further handicap from a suboptimal batting order spot (#8) and a negative park factor. If the precipitation outlook worsens, we are prepared to pivot to protect our daily game caps.",
